Z||000000||87ECO5||03-12-2001||03:27 PM||||Just brought my '87 economy coupe home from Ed Parks' shop.  He received the car three weeks ago with a 2.5 - he returned the car Saturday with a Grooms remanufactured 3.4 in the back!<P>In addition to the 3.4, the car also got a new clutch, new flywheel, new water pump, "newer" Isuzu transaxle, new poly cradle bushings, backlit main and auxiliary gauges, new free-flowing cat., new console skeleton, and various other parts (that I can't think of right now).<P>Final bill was a little over the 5K mark.<P>Next steps are to install the leather seat covers, 17" rims/low-profile tires, strut tower brace and remaining poly suspension components that I ordered back in January!<P>Hmmm ... I think I need to start a new thread:  "Let's hear from everyone with a V6!"    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   just kidding ...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87ECO5_360_wannabe_2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Cheever2||03-12-2001||04:07 PM||||That's great news!  Now you need to give us a recording of the sound and/or a video showing how it runs!<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||85gt||03-12-2001||04:25 PM||||Must be nice. I just got an e-mail from Ed. I want to do the same thing and he was telling me about yours. If you don't care tell me all about it. I would like to have mine changed, but Ed said it was like $2000 more to do it on a 4 cyl. vs a 6 cyl.. That sounds like a lot of difference. Well have fun and don't let the wife and kids take it over.||||reg||6
Z||000003||tgowens||03-12-2001||05:13 PM||||Scott, the only thing I can say is: ENJOY!!! -- Ed does good work and you will be pleased. (by the way -- answer my email!!)<P>85gt, it IS more to upgrade a 2.5 to a 3.4 than from a 2.8 to a 3.4 due to the fact that there are hoses and tubes to convert on the 4 cyl which are already set up on a 6 cyl......that and the fact that most everything from the heads up on a 2.8 will bolt on to a 3.4 -- there is nothing from a 2.5 that will bolt on to a 3.4 meaning you would have to buy the 2.8 parts (intakes, manifolds, wiring harness, ECM, etc.........) That is the reason for the difference in cost.........||||reg||1
Z||000004||85gt||03-12-2001||08:37 PM||||So I would be better off finding a decent 6cyl. and starting there, because I should be able to get one for around $1000-$1500. At least it seems that way to me. I can always change out body panels.||||reg||6
